# UI Craft & Design Context

## Studio homepage — current Infinite Website

- The controlling creative direction is `docs/infinite-website/NORTH_STAR_v1.2.md`: **restrained centered B → C**. Neither Liquid Glass, clay-card styling, translucent dashboard panels nor turquoise glow is a required aesthetic. **Do not add them merely because a reusable rule recommends a trend**.
- The opening becomes spatial only through visibly connected website-derived columns, surfaces, borders and perspective. Favor meaningful depth/occlusion over opacity tricks, empty tunnels, particle effects or gratuitous WebGL.
- Preserve a clear typographic hierarchy, contrast, readable intermediate frames, native reversible scroll, no-JS/reduced-motion fallback and uninterrupted access to genuine work/contact.
- Use motion and layout primitives (CSS transitions, scroll-linked techniques, or scoped JS/GSAP) when justified by measured accessibility, reverse determinism and browser performance. No blanket requirement for one animation engine.

## Reusable interface principles across products

- Prefer legible copy, obvious focus, keyboard operation, touch-safe targets and meaningful affordances. Never rely solely on hover.
- Responsive layout must accommodate localized EN, KA and NL strings without clipping or unstable transitions. Test all locale lengths.
- `oklch()`, CSS `@property`, container queries and view transitions are **optional techniques**, not mandatory style signatures. Use them only where browser support, readability and fallback are verified.
- Digital-card customizer/card visual styles have their own product-specific requirements. Do not transfer those to the studio homepage.
